2. ABSOLUTE ARCHITECTURAL RULES

These rules apply to every change.

A. Industry-neutral architecture

AI Workforce must work for businesses across industries.

Examples include:

- SaaS
- Healthcare
- Education
- Fashion
- Retail
- Professional services
- Real estate
- Manufacturing
- Hospitality
- Financial services

Never hardcode a specific tenant, industry, product, pricing model, business identity or business workflow into the generic Alpha engine.

Specifically eliminate inappropriate global defaults or fallbacks involving:

- AI Workforce
- Magnus Verity
- NOIRÉ
- VANTÉ
- Apex
- TheRoots
- Clothing businesses
- Any other demonstration tenant

These may exist as explicitly isolated test fixtures or official platform identity data.

They must never become universal tenant defaults.

B. Tenant isolation

Every tenant-owned resource must have an explicit, verified tenant ownership boundary.

This includes:

- Company Brain
- Widget configurations
- Conversations
- Visitors
- Visitor sessions
- Inquiries
- Handoffs
- Analytics
- Notifications
- Admin records
- Files
- Audit events
- Knowledge bases
- Integrations
- Settings
- Cache entries

Never trust a client-provided tenant ID as proof of ownership.

Resolve tenant identity from authenticated ownership or a verified server-side widget mapping.

C. Preserve the existing product

Do not:

- Rewrite the entire application unnecessarily.
- Replace working components with mock implementations.
- Delete features to make tests pass.
- Weaken security rules to bypass authorization failures.
- Introduce unnecessary dependencies.
- Introduce additional paid AI APIs.
- Replace the active Gemini-based Alpha architecture.
- Break existing routes, dashboards, widget integrations or onboarding.
- Remove useful functionality without proving it is unsafe and documenting the change.

Use targeted, backward-compatible migrations wherever possible.

D. No fake success

Never return:

- "db_confirmed: true" without verified durable persistence.
- "inquiry_registered: true" without successful registration.
- "email_dispatched: true" when no email was sent.
- Healthy service statuses without real health checks.
- Successful handoff statuses without persisted handoff records.
- Verified AI answers without actual grounding evidence.

If an operation fails, report its actual failure state.

